COPY public.attractions (id, destination_id, name, type, duration, best_time, description, created_at) FROM stdin;
2	1	Game drive	activity	half-day	Year-round; dry season June–October	Morning or afternoon 4x4 game drive for Big Five viewing.	2026-08-31 16:19:28.011957
3	1	Maasai village visit	cultural	2 hours	Year-round	Guided visit to a Maasai manyatta with cultural explanation and dance.	2026-08-31 16:19:28.238181
4	1	Hot air balloon safari	activity	3 hours	June–October	Dawn balloon flight over the reserve followed by a bush breakfast.	2026-08-31 16:19:28.460215
5	2	Elephant herds	wildlife	half-day	June–October and January–February	Large elephant families on the Amboseli swamps with Kilimanjaro as backdrop.	2026-08-31 16:19:28.71739
6	2	Observation Hill	viewpoint	1 hour	Year-round; clearest Kilimanjaro views at dawn	Panoramic lookout over the park, wetlands, and Mount Kilimanjaro.	2026-08-31 16:19:28.945773
7	3	Lake Nakuru flamingos and rhinos	wildlife	half-day	Year-round	Shores of Lake Nakuru for flamingos, both rhino species, and Rothschild giraffe.	2026-08-31 16:19:29.17924
8	4	Lake Naivasha boat ride	activity	1–2 hours	Year-round	Boat safari for hippos, fish eagles, and shoreline birdlife.	2026-08-31 16:19:29.409813
9	5	Mzima Springs	attraction	2 hours	Year-round	Crystal springs with underwater hippo and fish viewing in Tsavo West.	2026-08-31 16:19:29.638297
10	6	Red elephants of Tsavo	wildlife	half-day	June–October	Dust-red elephants along the Galana River in Tsavo East.	2026-08-31 16:19:29.864371
11	8	Serengeti endless plains	park	full-day	June–October (migration); year-round for resident game	Open-plain game viewing and seasonal wildebeest migration routes.	2026-08-31 16:19:30.088393
12	9	Ngorongoro Crater descent	park	full-day	June–October	Full-day crater floor game drive among dense Big Five populations.	2026-08-31 16:19:30.355474
13	10	Lake Manyara game drive	park	half-day	Year-round	Groundwater forest, tree-climbing lions, and flamingo-lined soda lake.	2026-08-31 16:19:30.580224
14	1	Maasai Mara National Reserve	park	Full day	Year-round; peak July–October	Kenya's finest wildlife sanctuary, with well over 450 recorded species and resident wildlife year-round in addition to the seasonal migration.	2026-09-07 17:26:12.988328
15	1	Great Wildebeest Migration	natural_phenomenon	Seasonal	July–September	Over a million wildebeest and zebra cross the Mara plains and the Mara River during the migration, drawing predators and dramatic river crossings.	2026-09-07 17:26:12.988328
16	1	Maasai Village (Manyatta) Visit	cultural	Half day (optional)	Year-round	Guided visit to a local Maasai village to learn about traditional homes, customs, and dances. Optional add-on, bookable in advance.	2026-09-07 17:26:12.988328
17	1	Hot Air Balloon Safari	activity	Early morning (optional)	Year-round	Sunrise hot air balloon float over the Mara plains for an aerial view of the wildlife and landscape, typically followed by a bush breakfast. Optional add-on, extra cost.	2026-09-07 17:26:12.988328
18	1	Guided Nature Walk	activity	1–2 hours (optional)	Year-round	Walking excursion near camp led by a guide, covering local flora, animal tracks, and bird life. Optional add-on.	2026-09-07 17:26:12.988328
64	4	Hell's Gate National Park	park	Half day	Dry season (Jun–Oct, Dec–Feb)	Renowned for dramatic cliffs, gorges, geothermal features, hot springs and steam vents. One of the few Kenyan parks where visitors can walk or cycle among wildlife, including zebra, buffalo, antelope, and rare vultures and eagles. Fischer's Tower (climbing) and Olkaria Geothermal Spa are nearby.	2026-09-08 19:02:41.850497
65	4	Crescent Island Game Sanctuary	wildlife_sanctuary	Half day (boat + walk)	Dry season (Jul–Oct, Jan–Mar)	Private, predator-free wildlife sanctuary on Lake Naivasha reached by boat, known for close walking safaris among giraffe, zebra, waterbuck and antelope, plus strong birdwatching.	2026-09-08 19:02:41.850497
66	4	Lake Naivasha Boat Ride	activity	1 hour (optional)	Year-round	Boat ride on Lake Naivasha, often combined with a Crescent Island visit.	2026-09-08 19:02:41.850497
67	7	David Sheldrick Wildlife Trust Nairobi Nursery	wildlife_sanctuary	1 hour	Daily public visiting hour (11:00am–12:00pm)	Elephant and rhino orphanage supporting Kenya's conservation work; the public visiting hour lets guests watch and learn about the hand-reared orphans.	2026-09-08 19:02:41.850497
68	7	Giraffe Centre (AFEW)	wildlife_sanctuary	1 hour	Daily, 9:00am–5:00pm	Conservation centre for the endangered Rothschild's giraffe, with a raised platform allowing visitors to feed and interact with giraffes up close.	2026-09-08 19:02:41.850497
63	3	Lake Nakuru Rhino Sanctuary & Bird Watching	park	Half day / Full day	Year-round	Game drive around the alkaline lake for flamingos, pelicans and other water birds, plus a dedicated black and white rhino sanctuary. Waterbuck, impala, buffalo and gazelle are found in the surrounding gardens.	2026-09-08 19:02:41.850497
