36	28	\N	9	angata-ngorongoro-camp	Angata Ngorongoro Camp	Nyati Special Campsite, eastern rim of the Ngorongoro Crater	Tanzania	["En-suite tents", "Lounge tent", "Dining tent", "Campfire", "Free coffee and tea", "Crater rim walks", "Bush lunch on the crater floor"]	A small tented camp on the eastern rim of the Ngorongoro Crater, close to Crater Lodge. It has eight guest tents, including a family unit made of two tents. Each tent has its own bathroom with a shower and flush toilet, and the beds can be set up as a king, twin or triple. Guests relax in the lounge tent with free Tanzanian coffee or tea, eat freshly cooked meals in the dining tent and gather around the campfire in the evening.	{"website": "https://www.angatacamps.com/ngorongoro", "totalRooms": 8, "elevationMeters": 2310}	2026-09-24 07:51:53.875401
37	28	\N	8	angata-serengeti-camp	Angata Serengeti Camp	Seronera, central Serengeti National Park	Tanzania	["En-suite tents", "Lounge tent", "Dining tent", "Campfire", "Free coffee and tea", "Bush lunches and dinners", "Balloon safari bookings"]	A large tented camp in Seronera, in the middle of the Serengeti, which makes game drives easy in almost every direction. It has twelve large guest tents, including a family unit made of two tents. Each tent has its own bathroom with a shower and flush toilet, and guests can ask for a king bed or two twin beds. There is a lounge tent with free Tanzanian coffee or tea, a dining tent serving freshly cooked meals, and a campfire in the evening. Seronera airstrip is about a 15 minute drive away.	{"website": "https://www.angatacamps.com/serengeti", "totalRooms": 12}	2026-09-24 07:51:53.875401
38	24	\N	1	masai-mara-sopa-lodge	Masai Mara Sopa Lodge	Oloolaimutia Hills, Masai Mara National Reserve	Kenya	["Swimming pool", "Restaurant", "Bar and lounge", "Outdoor boma dining area", "Wi-Fi in public areas", "Gift shop", "En-suite rooms with private verandas"]	One of the first safari lodges built in the Masai Mara, set high on the slopes of the Oloolaimutia Hills with views over the gardens and the reserve. The lodge has 99 rooms in round cottages with conical roofs, and each room has an en-suite bathroom, mosquito nets, a safe and a veranda. Public areas include a restaurant, an outdoor boma dining area, a bar, a lounge and a swimming pool.	{"website": "https://www.sopalodges.com/masai-mara-sopa-lodge", "totalRooms": 99, "nearestGate": "Oloolaimutia Gate"}	2026-09-24 07:51:53.875401
39	24	\N	3	lake-nakuru-sopa-lodge	Lake Nakuru Sopa Lodge	Lake Nakuru National Park	Kenya	["Infinity swimming pool with pool bar", "Restaurant", "Bar and lounge", "Wi-Fi in public areas", "Gift shop", "Guided nature walks", "Bush dining"]	A hillside lodge on the western edge of the Great Rift Valley with views over Lake Nakuru and the national park. It has about 60 rooms, a lounge, bar and dining room with sheltered outdoor terraces, and an infinity swimming pool that looks out over the lake. Guests can go on game drives, guided nature walks and bird watching, and the park is home to both white and black rhinos.	{"website": "https://www.sopalodges.com/lake-nakuru-sopa-lodge", "totalRooms": 60}	2026-09-24 08:49:44.951623
40	26	\N	1	zebra-plains-mara-camp	Zebra Plains Mara Camp	Below Oldonyo Oloip Ridge, Masai Mara	Kenya	["Swimming pool", "Spa", "Bar lounge", "Indoor and outdoor lounges", "Campfire areas", "Indoor and outdoor dining", "Wi-Fi in main area", "Private verandahs"]	A classic tented safari camp below the Oldonyo Oloip Ridge with wide views over the open plains of the Masai Mara. It has savannah facing and hillside facing rooms, plus family tents joined by a private lounge. Every room has its own bathroom with a hot shower, a study desk and a private verandah. The camp has a swimming pool, a spa, a bar lounge, indoor and outdoor lounges, campfire areas and three dining lounges, and a natural waterhole in front of the camp draws wildlife during the dry season.	{"checkIn": "12:00", "website": "https://zebraplainscollection.com/zebra-plains-mara-camp/", "checkOut": "10:00", "totalRooms": 48}	2026-09-24 08:49:44.951623
41	29	\N	12	baobab-beach-resort-diani	Baobab Beach Resort	Diani Beach Road, Diani, Kwale County	Kenya	["Beach access to Diani and Galu", "Swimming pools", "Spa", "Restaurants and bars", "Tropical gardens", "Rooms with balcony or terrace"]	A large beach resort set in tropical gardens dotted with baobab trees, with access to both Diani Beach and the quieter Galu Beach. Rooms have a private balcony or terrace with sea, pool or garden views. The resort has swimming pools, a spa, restaurants and bars, and a wide choice of beach activities.	{"website": "https://baobab-beach-resort.com"}	2026-09-24 08:49:44.951623
42	30	\N	13	sweetwaters-serena-camp	Sweetwaters Serena Camp	Ol Pejeta Conservancy, Laikipia plains	Kenya	["Heated swimming pool with pool bar", "Rhino Restaurant", "Waterhole bar", "Spa massages", "Recreation centre", "Free Wi-Fi", "En-suite tents with veranda or balcony"]	A tented camp inside Ol Pejeta Conservancy on the Laikipia plains, set around a waterhole with views of Mount Kenya. It has about 56 en-suite tents, each with a private veranda or balcony and free Wi-Fi. The camp has the Rhino Restaurant, a waterhole bar, a heated swimming pool with a pool bar, a spa for massages and a recreation centre with table tennis, foosball, darts and a pool table. The conservancy is home to the Big Five and to the last two northern white rhinos.	{"website": "https://www.serenahotels.com/sweetwaters", "totalRooms": 56}	2026-09-24 09:16:50.767351
43	27	\N	3	eagle-palace-hotel-nakuru	Eagle Palace Hotel	Oginga Odinga Road, Nakuru town	Kenya	["Restaurant", "Free parking", "Free Wi-Fi", "Terrace", "Conference facilities", "Tea and coffee making facilities"]	A hotel in the centre of Nakuru town on Oginga Odinga Road, used as an overnight stop on Lake Nakuru game drive days. It has an on site restaurant open from 7 am to 10 pm, free parking, a terrace and conference facilities. Rooms have a private bathroom with a shower and tea and coffee making facilities.	{"website": "https://eaglepalacehotel.com", "checkOut": "10:00"}	2026-09-24 09:16:50.767351
44	31	\N	4	dove-nest-lodge-naivasha	Dove Nest Lodge	North Kinangop Road, Naivasha	Kenya	["Swimming pool", "Restaurant", "Bush bar", "Manicured gardens", "Conference rooms", "Tea making facilities in rooms"]	A lodge along North Kinangop Road near Lake Naivasha, with rooms and cottages that have flat screen TVs, tea making facilities and extra bedding for cool nights. Meals are served in the restaurant, in the gardens or on the private balcony, and there is a bush bar and an outdoor swimming pool. It is a quiet base for boat rides on the lake and walks on Crescent Island.	{"website": "https://dovenestlodge.com"}	2026-09-24 09:16:50.767351
45	25	\N	2	nyati-safari-camp-amboseli	Nyati Safari Camp	Kimana Gate, Amboseli National Park	Kenya	["Restaurant with Kilimanjaro views", "Hot and cold showers", "Free Wi-Fi", "Tents and stone rooms"]	A budget friendly camp right beside Kimana Gate at the edge of Amboseli National Park, with views of Mount Kilimanjaro. Guests stay in spacious tents or stone rooms with private toilets and hot and cold showers. The camp has a restaurant with a view of Kilimanjaro and free Wi-Fi.	{"website": "https://www.nyatisafaricamp.com"}	2026-09-24 09:16:50.767351
