COPY public.tours (id, slug, title, short_title, destination, countries, duration, days, price, original_price, image, gallery, description, long_description, highlights, included, excluded, itinerary, rating, review_count, departing, difficulty, group_size, type, tier, recommended, featured, likes, created_at, company_id, child_price, infant_price) FROM stdin;
4	6-day-serengeti-ngorongoro-masai-mara	6-Day Serengeti, Ngorongoro & Masai Mara	Serengeti & Ngorongoro	Ngorongoro, Serengeti, Masai Mara	["Kenya", "Tanzania"]	6 Days / 5 Nights	6	1850	2100	["https://i.pinimg.com/1200x/21/22/c4/2122c4de122825863beba78c53078804.jpg", "https://i.pinimg.com/736x/71/75/64/717564b36cbc33a6e8c33edce55b2251.jpg", "/maasai_village.png", "/fun.png", "/zebras.png"]	["https://i.pinimg.com/1200x/21/22/c4/2122c4de122825863beba78c53078804.jpg", "https://i.pinimg.com/736x/71/75/64/717564b36cbc33a6e8c33edce55b2251.jpg", "/balloon_safari1.png", "/fun.png", "/zebras.png"]	Cross the border for the ultimate East African safari experience, from the Ngorongoro Crater to the Serengeti and Masai Mara.	This cross-border safari is the pinnacle of East African wildlife experiences. Descend into the Ngorongoro Crater, cross the vast Serengeti plains, and finish in Kenya's legendary Masai Mara. Six days of non-stop wildlife encounters across two countries.	["Ngorongoro Crater descent", "Serengeti endless plains", "Cross-border Tanzania to Kenya", "Big Five in multiple parks"]	["Cross-border transport in 4x4", "Full board accommodation", "All park entrance fees both countries", "Border crossing assistance", "Professional guide"]	["Tanzania and Kenya visas", "International flights", "Travel insurance", "Personal expenses"]	[{"day": 1, "title": "Arusha to Ngorongoro", "description": "Drive from Arusha to Ngorongoro Conservation Area. Settle at the crater rim lodge with breathtaking views."}, {"day": 2, "title": "Ngorongoro Crater", "description": "Descend into the crater for a full day of wildlife viewing. The crater floor hosts nearly 30,000 animals."}, {"day": 3, "title": "Ngorongoro to Serengeti", "description": "Cross the Serengeti plains, with game viewing en route. Arrive at the central Serengeti for afternoon game drive."}, {"day": 4, "title": "Full Day Serengeti", "description": "Full day exploring the Serengeti, following the migration if in season. Morning and afternoon game drives."}, {"day": 5, "title": "Serengeti to Masai Mara", "description": "Cross the border into Kenya and enter the Masai Mara for a sunset game drive."}, {"day": 6, "title": "Masai Mara to Nairobi", "description": "Final morning game drive, then return to Nairobi arriving late afternoon."}]	4.9	22	Daily	Moderate	2-7 persons	private	luxury	t	t	69	2026-02-26 23:04:54.121298	aha	\N	\N
22	8-day-lake-nakuru-masai-mara-diani-beach-safari	8 Days Masai Mara, Lake Nakuru & Diani Beach Safari from Nairobi | Mid Range Road and Train Tour	8 Day Mara, Nakuru & Diani Safari	Lake Nakuru, Masai Mara, Diani Beach	["Kenya"]	8 Days / 7 Nights	8	2132	\N	["/camels.png", "/marariver.png", "/murife.png", "/cubs.png", "/cheeting.png", "/migration.png"]	["/camels.png", "/ziwa-bush-lodge.png", "/cubs.png", "/marariver.png", "/cheeting.png", "/migration.png"]	An 8 day mid range Kenya safari that combines Lake Nakuru and the Masai Mara with three relaxing days at Diani Beach, with full board meals, a private 4x4 Land Cruiser, train tickets between Nairobi and Mombasa and all park fees.	This 8 day mid range safari takes you from the Great Rift Valley to the Masai Mara and finishes with a relaxed stay on the Indian Ocean coast at Diani Beach. You begin with a scenic drive from Nairobi, with stops at the Rift Valley viewpoint and the little Italian church, before an afternoon game drive at Lake Nakuru National Park. The park is known as a bird sanctuary because flamingos can cover the whole surface of the lake, and it is the only park in Kenya where you are sure to see both white and black rhinos. From Nakuru you drive to the Masai Mara National Reserve for three nights at Zebra Plains Mara Camp, with an afternoon game drive on arrival and two full days of game viewing, including a picnic lunch near the Mara River. The Mara is one of the few places where you can see all of the Big Five, and between July and October the plains fill with migrating wildebeest and zebras. On day five you return to Nairobi and take the afternoon train to Mombasa, where you are picked up and taken to Baobab Beach Resort in Diani for three nights on full board. You can swim, take a boat ride, watch birds, learn about Swahili culture or arrange a short fishing trip with local guides. On the last day you leave the resort to catch the afternoon train back to Nairobi. Game drives are in a private 4x4 Land Cruiser with a professional driver guide, and all park fees, train tickets and transfers are included.	["Afternoon game drive at Lake Nakuru National Park with flamingos and both white and black rhinos", "Three nights in the Masai Mara with two full days of game drives", "Chance to see the Great Migration in season, usually between July and October", "Comfortable train ride between Nairobi and Mombasa", "Three nights on full board at Baobab Beach Resort in Diani", "Private 4x4 Land Cruiser with a professional driver guide"]	["Services of a professional driver guide", "Pick up and drop off in Nairobi", "Game drives as per the itinerary", "Meals as in the itinerary", "Transport in a private 4x4 Land Cruiser", "All park entry fees", "Accommodation on safari and at the beach resort", "Train tickets between Nairobi and Mombasa", "Transfers to and from the train station and airport", "All other transfers in the itinerary", "Drinking water", "Government taxes"]	["Flight from Mombasa if needed", "Tips and gratuities", "International airfares", "Visas", "Optional hot air balloon ride in Masai Mara at 450 USD per person", "Optional Masai village visit at 25 USD per person", "Optional guided nature walk at 25 USD per person", "Soft drinks and local beers", "Any government imposed increase in taxes or park fees"]	[{"day": 1, "title": "Nairobi to Lake Nakuru National Park", "description": "Be picked up at your Nairobi hotel at 8 am and drive south along the Great Rift Valley, stopping at the viewpoint to admire the escarpment. A few minutes further on you will stop at the little Italian church, which was built by Italian workers during the construction of the road as a place to worship. You reach Nakuru in time for lunch at Lake Nakuru Sopa Lodge, followed by an afternoon game drive in Lake Nakuru National Park. The park is known as a bird sanctuary because the surface of the lake can be covered by lesser and greater flamingos. It is also famous for the Big Five without elephants, and it is the only park in Kenya where you are sure to see both white and black rhinos. Return to the lodge for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 2, "title": "Lake Nakuru to Masai Mara", "description": "Have breakfast at the lodge, then say goodbye to Nakuru and drive to the Masai Mara. You will be welcomed with lunch at the camp when you arrive, and after a short rest you head into the reserve for an afternoon game drive. The Mara is one of the few places left on earth where wildlife still lives in great numbers, much as it did when it roamed the plains and forests of Africa. As the northern tip of the vast Serengeti ecosystem, it hosts the spectacular seasonal migration of many thousands of wildebeest, zebras and the predators that follow them. Drive back to the camp in the evening for dinner and overnight at Zebra Plains Mara Camp."}, {"day": 3, "title": "Full Day in Masai Mara", "description": "Spend the day exploring the Masai Mara in depth. A packed lunch is served picnic style inside the park, close to the Mara River. The reserve is well known for its black maned lions and its resident wildlife, and it is one of the few places where you may see the Big Five during a single morning game drive. Many cheetahs here are so used to vehicles that they rest in the shade under them, and some even climb onto the roof for a better view of their prey. Return to the camp in the evening for dinner and overnight at Zebra Plains Mara Camp."}, {"day": 4, "title": "Full Day Game Drive in Masai Mara", "description": "After breakfast, leave at 6:30 am for a game drive that lasts until 6:30 pm, looking for wildlife you did not see the day before. Because nature cannot be predicted, you will cover different parts of the reserve and gain new experiences. The Masai Mara is the most famous reserve in Kenya because of its large wildlife population, and it is one of the few places where all of the Big Five are found. The park is also home to about 470 bird species and rare animals such as roan antelopes and nocturnal bat eared foxes, and you will see the lilac breasted roller, which is the national bird of Kenya. Return to the camp in the evening for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 5, "title": "Masai Mara to Nairobi and Diani Beach", "description": "After breakfast, drive back to Nairobi and be dropped off at the railway station to catch the 3 pm train to Mombasa. On arrival in Mombasa you will be picked up and taken to Baobab Beach Resort or a similar resort in Diani for your overnight stay."}, {"day": 6, "title": "Relax at Diani Beach", "description": "Have breakfast at the resort, then enjoy a day at the coast, which is home to the Swahili people of Kenya and rich in cultural heritage. Lunch is served at the resort, and you can spend the rest of the day on beach activities such as swimming, boat rides and bird watching, depending on what you have planned. Dinner and overnight are at the resort on a full board basis."}, {"day": 7, "title": "Beach Day at Diani", "description": "Enjoy breakfast in the comfort of your resort and carry on with the beach activities that the front office desk can arrange for you. You can take photos, or ask about short fishing trips along the coast for both beginners and experienced fishermen, which are arranged at a small fee agreed with the local guides. All meals and the overnight stay are at the resort."}, {"day": 8, "title": "Diani Beach to Nairobi", "description": "Wake up relaxed and have breakfast at your leisure. Then leave the resort to connect to the 3 pm train from Mombasa back to Nairobi, taking home the best memories to share with friends. This ends your safari."}]	4.8	30	Daily	Easy	2-7 persons	private	midrange	f	f	58	2026-09-24 08:49:44.951623	aha	1066	\N
