 day of game drives. Morning and afternoon sessions in different areas of the reserve, maximizing wildlife sightings."}, {"day": 5, "title": "Masai Mara to Nairobi", "description": "Final morning game drive, then return to Nairobi arriving late afternoon."}]	4.8	27	Daily	Easy	2-7 persons	private	budget	f	t	33	2026-02-26 23:04:53.410669	aha	\N	\N
23	9-day-ol-pejeta-nakuru-masai-mara-naivasha-amboseli-safari	9 Days Ol Pejeta, Lake Nakuru, Masai Mara, Lake Naivasha & Amboseli Safari from Nairobi | Mid Range Private Tour	9 Day Kenya Circuit Safari	Ol Pejeta, Lake Nakuru, Masai Mara, Lake Naivasha, Amboseli	["Kenya"]	9 Days / 8 Nights	9	2150	\N	["/kili.png", "/lioness.png", "/flams.png", "/cheeting.png"]	["/kili.png", "/lioness.png", "/flams.png"]	A 9 day mid range private safari that covers five of the best wildlife areas in Kenya: Ol Pejeta Conservancy, Lake Nakuru, the Masai Mara, Lake Naivasha and Amboseli, with a private 4x4 Land Cruiser, meals as in the itinerary and all park fees.	This 9 day safari is a complete tour of Kenya, taking you from the plains of Laikipia to the slopes of Mount Kilimanjaro. You start with a scenic drive north to Ol Pejeta Conservancy, a wildlife sanctuary where you can see lions, elephants, buffaloes, giraffes and rhinos on an afternoon game drive. Next comes Lake Nakuru National Park, a haven for birds and rhinos where thousands of flamingos can turn the shoreline pink. You then spend three nights in the Masai Mara, one of the best places in Africa to see big game, with game drives every day and a full day exploring the plains and the Mara River. Between July and September the grasslands are covered with wildebeest, zebras and gazelles during the great migration. From the Mara you travel to Lake Naivasha for a boat safari among hippos and fish eagles and a walk on Crescent Island, where you can stroll among zebras, giraffes and antelopes with no predators around. The safari ends with two nights in Amboseli, where large herds of elephants walk against the backdrop of Mount Kilimanjaro, and you can climb Observation Hill for a view over the swamps and plains. Transport is in a private 4x4 Land Cruiser with a professional driver guide, and you are dropped off at your preferred location in Nairobi at the end.	["Big Five game viewing in Ol Pejeta Conservancy including rhinos", "Flamingos, white and black rhinos and Rothschild giraffes at Lake Nakuru", "Three nights in the Masai Mara with game drives every day", "Boat safari on Lake Naivasha and a walk among wildlife on Crescent Island", "Elephants against Mount Kilimanjaro and Observation Hill views in Amboseli", "Private 4x4 Land Cruiser with a professional driver guide"]	["Accommodation as per the itinerary", "Meals as in the itinerary", "Transport in a private 4x4 Land Cruiser", "Game drives and park activities", "Park and conservation fees", "Government taxes and levies", "Bottled drinking water", "Services of a professional driver guide"]	["International and domestic flights", "Travel documentation such as visas and travel insurance", "Personal expenses", "Tips and gratuities", "Optional and personal activities", "Optional hot air balloon safari in Masai Mara at 430 USD per person"]	[{"day": 1, "title": "Nairobi to Ol Pejeta Conservancy", "description": "Leave Nairobi in the morning and head north towards Ol Pejeta Conservancy, a renowned wildlife sanctuary in Laikipia. Enjoy the scenic views of central Kenya on the way, and arrive at your camp in time for lunch. In the afternoon, set out on an exciting game drive, where you have the chance to see lions, elephants, buffaloes, giraffes and rhinos in their natural habitat. Return to the camp for dinner and overnight at Sweetwaters Serena Camp."}, {"day": 2, "title": "Ol Pejeta Conservancy to Lake Nakuru National Park", "description": "After breakfast, leave Ol Pejeta and travel to Lake Nakuru National Park, a haven for birds and rhinos. Arrive in time for lunch, then head out in the afternoon on a game drive around the lake, where thousands of flamingos can turn the shoreline pink. Keep an eye out for white and black rhinos, Rothschild giraffes and the elusive leopard. As the sun sets, return for dinner and a restful night at Eagle Palace Hotel."}, {"day": 3, "title": "Lake Nakuru to Masai Mara National Reserve", "description": "Leave for the Masai Mara in the morning and check in at your camp on arrival for lunch. After a little rest, enjoy an afternoon of wildlife viewing in the reserve, which has an abundance of wildlife and big game. The spectacular wildebeest migration takes place from July to September, when the grasslands are covered with a mass of wildebeest, zebras and gazelles, and large predators arrive to take advantage of the prey. Return to the camp in the evening for dinner and overnight at Enchoro Wildlife Camp."}, {"day": 4, "title": "Full Day in Masai Mara National Reserve", "description": "Have an early breakfast and head out for a game drive in the legendary Masai Mara. The reserve is home to an abundance of wildlife, including lions, cheetahs, elephants, buffaloes and zebras. Return to the camp for lunch, then set out again for an afternoon game drive. After an exhilarating day, return to the camp for dinner and overnight at Enchoro Wildlife Camp."}, {"day": 5, "title": "Full Day Game Drive in Masai Mara", "description": "Spend the whole day exploring the vast plains of the Masai Mara on game drives. With a packed lunch, venture deep into the reserve in search of the Big Five and other iconic animals. Visit the Mara River, where crocodiles and hippos thrive and, if you are lucky, you may witness dramatic predator and prey encounters. Return to the camp in the evening for a well earned dinner and overnight rest."}, {"day": 6, "title": "Masai Mara to Lake Naivasha", "description": "After breakfast, say goodbye to the Masai Mara and travel to Lake Naivasha, arriving in time for lunch. Spend the afternoon exploring this peaceful lake. One of the highlights is a boat safari, where you can get close to hippos, fish eagles and other bird species. Crescent Island offers the chance to walk among grazing zebras, giraffes and antelopes in an environment with no predators. Enjoy the evening at your lodge, soaking in the calm atmosphere of the lake, with dinner and overnight at Dove Nest Lodge."}, {"day": 7, "title": "Lake Naivasha to Amboseli National Park", "description": "Have an early breakfast before leaving for Amboseli National Park, which lies at the foot of the majestic Mount Kilimanjaro. Arrive in time for lunch at your camp, then head out on an afternoon game drive. Amboseli is best known for its large herds of elephants, often seen against the backdrop of the highest mountain in Africa. Return to the camp in the evening, where you can relax and enjoy stunning sunset views of Kilimanjaro. Dinner and overnight at Nyati Safari Camp."}, {"day": 8, "title": "Full Day in Amboseli National Park", "description": "After breakfast, spend a full day in Amboseli with morning and afternoon game drives. Capture breathtaking views of elephants walking against the backdrop of Kilimanjaro, one of the most iconic sights in Africa. Visit Observation Hill for a panoramic view of the park and its varied landscapes, including the swamps where hippos and water birds thrive. Dinner and overnight at Nyati Safari Camp."}, {"day": 9, "title": "Amboseli National Park to Nairobi", "description": "After breakfast, begin your journey back to Nairobi, where you will be dropped off at your preferred location. This marks the end of an extraordinary 9 day Kenya safari, and you head home with endless sweet memories."}]	4.8	30	Daily	Easy	2-7 persons	private	midrange	f	f	42	2026-09-24 09:16:50.767351	aha	1075	\N
