21	6-day-ngorongoro-serengeti-masai-mara-mid-range-safari	6 Days Ngorongoro, Serengeti & Masai Mara Mid Range Safari from Nairobi | Angata & Sopa Lodges	Ngorongoro, Serengeti & Mara Safari	Ngorongoro Crater, Serengeti, Masai Mara	["Kenya", "Tanzania"]	6 Days / 5 Nights	6	3682	\N	["/serengeti.png", "/cubs.png", "/migration.png"]	["/serengeti.png", "/cubs.png", "/migration.png"]	A private 6 day mid range safari from Nairobi through Ngorongoro Crater, the Serengeti and the Masai Mara, staying at Angata and Sopa lodges, with full board meals, park fees and a private 4x4 Land Cruiser.	This 6 day safari takes you across the border from Kenya into Tanzania and back again, visiting three of the most famous wildlife areas in Africa. You start in Nairobi and are driven to the Namanga border, where your guide meets you and takes you to the Ngorongoro Crater, a huge natural bowl packed with wildlife. From there you travel to the Serengeti, whose name means endless plains in the Maasai language, and spend a full day exploring its grasslands, home to lions, leopards, cheetahs and vast herds of plains game. You then cross back into Kenya through Isebania and finish with a full day in the Masai Mara, where you may see the Great Migration depending on the season. You stay in comfortable mid range camps and lodges, with meals, park fees and drinking water all included. Transport is in a private 4x4 Land Cruiser with a professional English speaking driver guide, and the safari ends with a scenic drive back to Nairobi.	["A full day on the floor of Ngorongoro Crater", "A full day exploring the Serengeti plains", "Cross border safari between Tanzania and Kenya", "A full day of game viewing in the Masai Mara", "Chance to see the Great Migration, depending on the season", "Private 4x4 Land Cruiser with an English speaking driver guide"]	["Accommodation as per the itinerary", "All meals as specified in the itinerary", "All park entrance fees", "Transport in a private 4x4 Land Cruiser", "Bottled drinking water", "Transfer to the Namanga border", "Government taxes", "Professional English speaking driver guide", "Game drives as per the itinerary"]	["International and domestic flights", "Visa fees", "Accommodation for the first night in Nairobi", "Personal expenses", "Travel insurance", "Optional activities such as the hot air balloon safari in the Masai Mara", "Tips and gratuities", "Soft drinks and local beers"]	[{"day": 1, "title": "Nairobi to Ngorongoro Crater", "description": "You are picked up from your hotel in Nairobi at 5 am and driven to the Namanga border, where your guide meets you. From there you drive to Ngorongoro Crater for a day of game viewing on the crater floor. You stop for a picnic lunch at the Ngoitoktok Springs picnic site. All of the Big Five may be seen here, along with cheetahs, Grants and Thomsons gazelles, zebras, wildebeest and spotted hyenas, and flamingos are sometimes seen on the crater lake. Dinner and overnight at Angata Ngorongoro Camp in the Nyati area."}, {"day": 2, "title": "Ngorongoro Crater to Serengeti National Park", "description": "After breakfast, leave Ngorongoro and drive across the beautiful Ngorongoro highlands before descending into the vast Serengeti plains. The Serengeti is famous for its endless grasslands and its huge numbers of wildlife. You enjoy game drives as you enter the park, where you may spot elephants, giraffes and possibly a leopard. You arrive at your camp in the late afternoon, relax for a while, then go out on an evening game drive. Dinner and overnight at Angata Serengeti Camp."}, {"day": 3, "title": "Full Day in the Serengeti", "description": "After breakfast, spend the whole day exploring the Serengeti plains on game drives. This UNESCO World Heritage Site is home to the Big Five and a great variety of other wildlife. The central plains are a good place to find leopards, hyenas and cheetahs. The park is also the main stage for the yearly migration of wildebeest and zebras between the Serengeti and the Masai Mara. Eagles, flamingos, ducks, geese and vultures are among the birds you may see. Enjoy a picnic lunch in the bush before exploring other parts of the park, then return to your camp in the evening for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 4, "title": "Serengeti to Masai Mara National Reserve", "description": "After an early breakfast, leave the camp for a last game drive on your way out of the Serengeti. You drive to Isebania for immigration formalities, with a packed lunch along the way. As you enter the Masai Mara you enjoy more game viewing across its rolling savannahs, which are known for their wildlife and dramatic encounters between predators and prey. You arrive at your lodge in the evening for dinner and overnight at Masai Mara Sopa Lodge."}, {"day": 5, "title": "Full Day in the Masai Mara", "description": "After breakfast, spend the full day on game drives across the rich grasslands and rolling hills of the Masai Mara, Kenya's most celebrated safari destination. The Mara is known for its great herds of plains game, black maned lions, leopards and cheetahs, as well as many elephants and almost every kind of wildlife found in Kenya. Depending on the season, you may witness the Great Migration, when millions of wildebeest and zebras cross the Mara River in search of fresh grazing. Enjoy a picnic lunch by the river or under an acacia tree before an afternoon game drive, then return to your lodge for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 6, "title": "Masai Mara to Nairobi", "description": "After breakfast, leave the Masai Mara and drive back to Nairobi. Enjoy the scenic drive across the Rift Valley, with lunch on the way, and arrive in Nairobi in the late afternoon with happy memories of your safari. End of safari."}]	4.8	21	Daily	Moderate	2-7 persons	private	midrange	f	f	37	2026-09-24 07:30:55.343853	aha	\N	\N
