18	4-day-masai-mara-group-joining-safari	4 Days Masai Mara Group Joining Safari from Nairobi | Enchoro Wildlife Camp	4 Day Mara Group Safari	Masai Mara	["Kenya"]	4 Days / 3 Nights	4	1392	\N	["/ewc-tent-superior.png", "/murife2.png", "/leophant.png", "/volunt.png"]	["/ewc-tent-superior.png", "/murife2.png", "/volunt.png", "/leophant.png"]	Join a group of fellow travelers on a 4 day Masai Mara safari with three nights at Enchoro Wildlife Camp, two full days of game drives, and road transfers from Nairobi.	This 4 day group joining safari is made for travelers who want the full Masai Mara experience at a shared cost. You will be picked up from your Nairobi hotel in the morning and travel with a small group in a customized safari van with a pop up roof, driving along the Great Rift Valley with a stop at a viewpoint for photos and a chance to meet local artisans. Three nights are spent at Enchoro Wildlife Camp, giving you extra time in the reserve compared to a shorter safari. You will enjoy an afternoon game drive on arrival day, a full day exploring the savannah with a picnic lunch, and another full day from early morning to sunset covering different parts of the reserve in search of wildlife you may have missed. The Masai Mara is Kenya's most famous reserve, one of the few places where all of the Big Five can be found, with 470 bird species and rare animals such as roan antelopes and bat eared foxes. On the final day, after an early breakfast, you drive back to Nairobi for your drop off, concluding the safari with sweet memories to carry home.	["Group joining safari with shared transport and costs", "Three nights at Enchoro Wildlife Camp", "Afternoon game drive on arrival day", "Two full days of game drives in the reserve", "Big Five and 470 bird species recorded", "Optional visit to a Maasai village"]	["Park entrance fees", "All meals as per the itinerary", "All transport in a customized safari van with a pop up roof", "Accommodation", "Bottled water", "Game drives as per the itinerary"]	["Gratuities and tips", "Drinks such as alcohol and beers", "Extra activities such as the hot air balloon safari and Maasai village visit"]	[{"day": 1, "title": "Nairobi to Masai Mara", "description": "Be picked up at your hotel by 8 am by your safari tour guide and meet the rest of the group. Transfer to the Masai Mara on a drive of five to six hours, passing along the Great Rift Valley with scenic views and a short stop at a viewpoint for photos. You will also interact with the locals and get a chance to buy some beautiful and unique handmade pieces. Arrive in time for lunch after checking in at the camp. In the afternoon, go out for a game drive in search of animals such as lions, wildebeest, cape buffalo, gazelles, leopards, African elephants and cheetahs, among others. In the evening, head back to your camp for dinner and overnight at Enchoro Wildlife Camp."}, {"day": 2, "title": "Full Day Game Drive in Masai Mara", "description": "After an early breakfast at the lodge, depart for a full day game drive in the Masai Mara National Reserve, carrying packed picnic lunch boxes. Explore the savannah in the morning in search of lions, cheetahs, elephants, buffalo and giraffes, while herds of wildebeest, zebras and gazelles graze in the golden morning light. Drive across the open plains and visit areas around the Talek or Mara Rivers to see hippos and crocodiles. Enjoy a picnic lunch served at a scenic spot inside the reserve, often under an acacia tree or near the riverbank, then continue deeper into the reserve as elephants cool off, buffalo gather in herds and predators prepare for their evening hunts. Conclude the day with a slow game drive back to camp, capturing sunset scenes across the savannah. An optional cultural visit to a Maasai village can be arranged at extra cost. Dinner and overnight at Enchoro Wildlife Camp."}, {"day": 3, "title": "Full Day Game Drive in Masai Mara", "description": "After breakfast, leave for an early game drive from 6:30 am to 6:30 pm in search of wildlife you never got a chance to view the previous day. You will cover different parts of the reserve, because nature is unpredictable and every day brings new experiences. The Masai Mara is Kenya's most famous reserve thanks to its large populations of wildlife, and it is one of the few places where all of the Big Five can be found. The park also boasts 470 bird species and rare animals such as roan antelopes and nocturnal bat eared foxes, along with the beautiful lilac breasted roller, Kenya's national bird. Return to the camp in the evening for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 4, "title": "Masai Mara to Nairobi", "description": "After an early breakfast at your camp, check out and depart the Masai Mara for Nairobi. Arrive in Nairobi and be dropped off at your hotel or the airport. This concludes your safari, with sweet memories to carry home."}]	4.5	44	Daily	Easy	6-12 persons	group	budget	f	f	52	2026-09-18 17:32:24.985234	aha	\N	\N
16	3-day-amboseli-safari-drop-off-diani	3 Days Amboseli Safari from Nairobi to Diani Beach | Nyati Safari Camp	Amboseli to Diani Safari	Amboseli, Diani	["Kenya"]	3 Days / 2 Nights	3	670	\N	["/Nyati-Safari-Camp.png", "/leophant.png", "/kili.png", "/camels.png"]	["/leophant.png", "/amboseli_elephants.png", "/kili.png", "/amboseli1.png", "/amboseli2.png"]	A 3 day Amboseli safari with two nights at Nyati Safari Camp, daily game drives with Mount Kilimanjaro views, and a beach drop off in Diani at the end.	This 3 day safari combines the best of bush and beach. Starting from Nairobi, you travel to Amboseli National Park, famous as one of the best places in the world to get close to free ranging elephants, with the majestic Mount Kilimanjaro, Africa's highest peak, as a dramatic backdrop. You will spend two nights at Nyati Safari Camp Amboseli and enjoy daily game drives across the open savannah, where lions, giraffes, zebras and all members of the Big Five can be seen throughout the year. The park also records more than 470 bird species, many of them raptors. After a final morning in the park, the journey continues south with lunch on the way and ends with a drop off at your beach hotel in Diani, leaving you with memories to last a lifetime.	["Close encounters with free ranging elephants", "Stunning views of Mount Kilimanjaro", "All members of the Big Five seen year round", "Early morning and afternoon game drives", "More than 470 recorded bird species", "Drop off at your beach hotel in Diani"]	["Services of a professional driver guide", "Pick up in Nairobi and drop off in Diani", "Game drives as per the itinerary", "Meals as in the itinerary", "Transport in a private 4x4 Land Cruiser", "All park entry fees", "Accommodation at Nyati Safari Camp Amboseli", "Drinking water", "Government taxes"]	["Tips and gratuities", "International airfares", "Visas", "Optional nature walk at 20 USD per person", "Optional Masai village visit at 25 USD per person", "Optional hot air balloon safari at 450 USD per person", "Soft drinks and local beers"]	[{"day": 1, "title": "Nairobi to Amboseli National Park", "description": "You will be picked up from your hotel in Nairobi early in the morning at 8 am and depart for Amboseli National Park, arriving in time for a relaxed lunch at Nyati Safari Camp. In the afternoon, head out for your first game drive. This is the final catch of the day for many animals, which come out of their hides to feed and bask in the sun, while kobs and other grazers gather before their night's rest. Amboseli is famous as the best place in the world to get close to free ranging elephants, and the park enjoys wonderful views of Mount Kilimanjaro, the highest free standing mountain in the world. Return to the camp for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 2, "title": "Full Day in Amboseli National Park", "description": "Set out early for a morning game drive to catch the African sunrise, when the animals are most active and fresh as they search for food in the open savannah grassland. Continue with a full day of game viewing with a packed picnic lunch. As the day warms up, many animals gather near the river banks to drink and cool down, while the big cats are rarely spotted until the sun goes down. Amboseli is home to all members of the Big Five, found here all year round, and more than 470 bird species have been recorded, around 60 of them raptors. Dinner and overnight at Nyati Safari Camp."}, {"day": 3, "title": "Amboseli National Park to Diani", "description": "Wake up early, enjoy breakfast at the camp, and leave for Diani at 9 am. You will have lunch along the way, after which you will be dropped off at your hotel in Diani with lots of good memories. End of safari."}]	4.7	41	Daily	Easy	2-7 persons	private	budget	f	f	18	2026-09-18 15:36:40.866299	aha	\N	\N
11	6-day-masai-mara-lake-nakuru-lake-naivasha-road-safari	6 Days Masai Mara, Lake Nakuru & Lake Naivasha Safari | Hot Air Balloon Included	Mara, Nakuru & Naivasha Safari	Masai Mara, Lake Nakuru, Lake Naivasha	["Kenya"]	6 Days / 5 Nights	6	2520	\N	["/mara_morning.png", "/destination_maasai_mara2.png", "/zebs.png", "/ewc-luxury-tent.png", "/bufalloes-in-african.png", "/hippos.png"]	["mara_morning.png", "/amboseli1.png", "/baboon_family.png", "/amboseli2.png", "/double_room.png"]	A private 6 day Kenya road safari combining the Masai Mara, Lake Nakuru and Lake Naivasha, with a hot air balloon flight, full board meals and transport in a 4x4 Land Cruiser.	This 6 day road safari is a classic Kenyan journey through three of the country's most rewarding destinations. It begins with two nights in the Masai Mara National Reserve, where you go in search of the Big Five across plains that host more than 450 recorded animal species and, between July and September, the great herds of the migration. A highlight of the trip is a hot air balloon flight over the Mara at sunrise, followed by a champagne style breakfast in the bush and a certificate from your captain. From the Mara the safari continues to Lake Nakuru National Park, a rhino sanctuary famous for its flamingos, pelicans and rich birdlife. You then travel to the fresh waters of Lake Naivasha for a night before a final day at Hell's Gate National Park, one of the few parks in Kenya where you can walk or cycle among zebra, buffalo and antelope. The safari ends with a drive back to Nairobi arriving in the late afternoon. Transport throughout is in a private 4x4 Land Cruiser with an English speaking driver guide.	["Two nights in the Masai Mara with daily game drives", "Hot air balloon safari over the Mara with bush breakfast", "Flamingos, rhinos and birdlife at Lake Nakuru", "Hell's Gate National Park where you can walk or cycle among wildlife", "Private 4x4 Land Cruiser with English speaking driver guide", "Optional Crescent Island walking safari on Lake Naivasha"]	["Services of a professional English speaking driver guide", "Meals as in the itinerary", "Transport in a 4x4 Land Cruiser", "All park entry fees as per the itinerary", "Accommodation in budget tented camps while on safari", "Drinking water", "Hot air balloon safari with bush breakfast", "Government taxes"]	["Tips and gratuities", "International airfares", "Visas", "Optional nature walk at 20 USD per person", "Optional Masai village visit at 25 USD per person", "Soft drinks and local beers"]	[{"day": 0, "title": "Nairobi City Visit", "description": "Before the safari begins, enjoy a visit to the Sheldrick Wildlife Trust Nairobi Nursery, where orphaned elephants and rhinos are cared for, followed by a stop at the Giraffe Centre. These visits are included in the package and can be arranged on the day before departure."}, {"day": 1, "title": "Nairobi to Masai Mara National Reserve", "description": "Set off from your Nairobi hotel at 7:30 am, heading down into the Great Rift Valley with a quick stop to admire the view from the escarpment. A second stop in Narok town allows you to pick up any personal items you may need, as this is the last major town before the reserve. Arrive at the Masai Mara in good time for lunch at the camp, then head out in the afternoon for your first game drive in search of the Big Five. Return to camp for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 2, "title": "Full Day in Masai Mara", "description": "After breakfast, spend the full day on game drives across the reserve, which is home to an amazing concentration of wildlife and more than 450 recorded species. Between July and September the Mara plains fill with migrating wildebeest and zebra, while resident wildlife can be seen all year round. Lunch is served in the park near the Mara River, the famous crossing point during the migration. Return to camp for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 3, "title": "Masai Mara Hot Air Balloon Safari", "description": "Wake very early for a transfer to the balloon launch site and lift off for an approximately one hour flight over the Mara plains. On landing, enjoy a champagne style picnic breakfast in the bush and receive your flight certificate from the captain. Rejoin your driver guide for a full day game drive to spot wildlife you may have missed, or return to camp for lunch and spend the afternoon on an optional guided visit to a Maasai village or a nature walk with Maasai guides. Dinner and overnight at the camp."}, {"day": 4, "title": "Masai Mara to Lake Nakuru National Park", "description": "After breakfast, leave the camp and drive to Lake Nakuru National Park with lunch served on the way. The lake offers the chance to see hundreds of bird species, including lesser and greater flamingos and pelicans, and the park is also a rhino sanctuary. Waterbuck, impala, buffalo and gazelle are often seen in the surrounding bush. Dinner and overnight at a hotel in Nakuru town."}, {"day": 5, "title": "Lake Nakuru to Lake Naivasha", "description": "After breakfast, head out for an extensive morning game drive in Lake Nakuru National Park, famous for the flocks of flamingos and other water birds that gather along its shores. Leave Nakuru after a late lunch and drive to Lake Naivasha for dinner and overnight at a hotel by the lake."}, {"day": 6, "title": "Lake Naivasha to Nairobi", "description": "After breakfast, visit Hell's Gate National Park, known for its dramatic landscapes, towering cliffs, gorges, geothermal features, hot springs and steam vents. It is one of the few parks in Kenya where visitors can walk or cycle among wildlife, and you may spot zebra, buffalo, antelope and rare birds such as vultures and eagles. You can also climb Fischer's Tower or relax at the nearby Olkaria Geothermal Spa. An optional boat ride on Lake Naivasha or a walking safari on Crescent Island, where giraffe, zebra and waterbuck roam freely, can be arranged before you leave for Nairobi with lunch on the way, arriving in the late afternoon as the safari ends."}]	4.8	34	Daily	Easy	2-7 persons	private	budget	f	f	21	2026-09-17 21:20:14.153827	aha	\N	\N
19	5-day-lake-nakuru-lake-naivasha-masai-mara-mid-comfort-safari	5 Days Lake Nakuru, Lake Naivasha & Masai Mara Mid Range Safari	Nakuru, Naivasha & Mara Mid Range	Lake Nakuru, Lake Naivasha, Masai Mara	["Kenya"]	5 Days / 4 Nights	5	1400	\N	["/1beach.png", "/ziwa-bush-lodge.png", "/cheeting.png"]	["/1beach.png", "/ziwa-bush-lodge.png", "/cheeting.png"]	A 5 day mid range safari combining Lake Nakuru, Hell's Gate and Lake Naivasha with two nights in the Masai Mara, staying at Sopa lodges and Zebra Plains Mara Camp.	This 5 day safari blends three of Kenya's most loved destinations with comfortable mid range accommodation throughout. The journey begins at Lake Nakuru National Park, a bird sanctuary where the alkaline lake is often ringed with lesser and greater flamingos, and the only park in Kenya where you are assured of seeing both white and black rhinos. From Nakuru you continue to Lake Naivasha for a visit to Hell's Gate National Park, where dramatic cliffs, geothermal springs and the striking Hell's Gate Gorge can be explored on foot, by bicycle or through rock climbing, and wildlife such as zebras and giraffes roams free of large predators. You then drive through Narok town to the Masai Mara National Reserve for two nights at Zebra Plains Mara Camp, with an afternoon game drive on arrival, a full day in the reserve with a picnic lunch at the Mara River, and a final optional visit to a Maasai village before returning to Nairobi. Between July and October the Mara plains host the great migration as wildebeest and zebras cross over from the Serengeti. Transport is in a private 4x4 Land Cruiser with a professional driver guide throughout.	["Rhinos and flamingos at Lake Nakuru National Park", "Hell's Gate National Park explored on foot or by bicycle", "Two nights in the Masai Mara at Zebra Plains Mara Camp", "Full day game drive with picnic lunch at the Mara River", "Great Migration crossings between July and October", "Comfortable mid range lodges throughout"]	["Services of a professional driver guide", "Pick up and drop off in Nairobi", "Game drives as per the itinerary", "Meals as in the itinerary", "Transport in a private 4x4 Land Cruiser", "All park entry fees", "Accommodation on safari", "Transfers to and from JKIA airport", "All other transfers in the itinerary", "Drinking water", "Government taxes"]	["International flights and any pre or post tour accommodation", "Tips for your driver guide at 10 USD per person per day", "Personal expenses such as souvenirs and travel insurance", "Any government imposed increases in taxes or park fees", "Single room supplement at an extra cost", "Visas", "Soft drinks and local beers", "Optional boat safari or Crescent Island walk", "Optional hot air balloon ride in Masai Mara at 450 USD per person", "Optional Masai village visit at 20 USD per person", "Optional guided nature walk at 25 USD per person"]	[{"day": 1, "title": "Nairobi to Lake Nakuru", "description": "Depart Nairobi at 7:30 am and drive southwards via the Rift Valley viewpoint, where you will admire the escarpment. Just a few meters ahead, stop at the little Italian church, which was built by Italian prisoners during the construction of the road so that they could worship. Arrive in Nakuru in time for lunch, then head out for an afternoon game drive in Lake Nakuru National Park, a bird sanctuary where the entire surface of the lake can be covered by lesser and greater flamingos. The park is also famous for the Big Five excluding elephants, and it is the only park in Kenya where you are assured of seeing both the white and the black rhinos. Return to the lodge for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 2, "title": "Lake Nakuru to Lake Naivasha", "description": "After breakfast, leave your lodge for the short drive to Lake Naivasha and visit Hell's Gate National Park, renowned for its dramatic landscapes, towering cliffs, geothermal springs and the striking Hell's Gate Gorge. Unlike most national parks, it offers a more interactive experience where you can explore on foot, by bicycle or through rock climbing, and it is home to zebras, giraffes and various bird species, though it lacks large predators. An optional boat ride on Lake Naivasha can be arranged. Dinner and overnight at your lodge or resort by the lake."}, {"day": 3, "title": "Lake Naivasha to Masai Mara", "description": "After breakfast, drive via Narok town to the Masai Mara National Reserve, arriving in time for lunch at your camp. In the afternoon, proceed for a game drive exploring the reserve in search of the Big Five. With more than 450 bird species recorded here, there is much to see, including rhinos, leopards, elephants, buffalo, wildebeest, zebras, warthogs, jackals, lions, many types of antelopes, crocodiles and giraffes, whether you are a game lover or a birding enthusiast. Return to your camp for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 4, "title": "Full Day in Masai Mara", "description": "After breakfast, leave the camp for a whole day game drive in the park, where you will enjoy and admire the great wildlife that inhabits this unique reserve. The zebras and wildebeest migrate from the Serengeti in Tanzania to Kenya and back again, and this migration takes place from July to October each year. Have your picnic lunch at the Mara River as you admire the fantastic wildlife, with several other animals also present, such as lions, giraffes, antelopes, gazelles and oryx. Return to your tented camp for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 5, "title": "Masai Mara to Nairobi", "description": "After breakfast, you have the option of visiting a Maasai village, where you will learn about the pristine culture of the Maasai tribe. Afterwards, drive back to Nairobi and be dropped off at JKIA airport or your preferred drop off point within the city."}]	4.8	61	Daily	Easy	2-7 persons	private	midrange	f	f	22	2026-09-21 08:19:06.486317	aha	\N	\N
20	6-day-masai-mara-lake-nakuru-lake-naivasha-migration-safari	6 Days Masai Mara Migration Safari with Lake Nakuru & Lake Naivasha	Mara Migration Safari	Masai Mara, Lake Nakuru, Lake Naivasha	["Kenya"]	6 Days / 5 Nights	6	2625	\N	["/marariver.png", "/migration.png", "/curio.png", "/mara_morning.png", "/zebs.png"]	["/curio.png", "/mara_morning.png", "/marariver.png", "/migration.png"]	A 6 day private migration safari with four nights in the Masai Mara at Zebra Plains Mara Camp, a night at Lake Nakuru Sopa Lodge, and a boat ride on Lake Naivasha before returning to Nairobi.	This 6 day safari is built around the great wildebeest migration, giving you more time in the Masai Mara than a standard itinerary. After an early departure from Nairobi through the Great Rift Valley, you spend four nights at Zebra Plains Mara Camp or a similar camp, with an afternoon game drive on arrival followed by three full days in the reserve from early morning to sunset. Long days in the Mara mean a real chance of witnessing the migration crossings at the Mara River between July and October, and the reserve is one of the few places where all of the Big Five can be found, alongside 470 bird species and rare animals such as roan antelopes and bat eared foxes. The safari then continues to Lake Nakuru National Park, a rhino sanctuary where the alkaline lake attracts hundreds of bird species including flamingos and pelicans, for a night at Lake Nakuru Sopa Lodge or similar. The final day is spent at Lake Naivasha, where a boat ride brings you close to hippos, before driving back to Nairobi. Throughout, you have exclusive use of a 4x4 safari Land Cruiser with a pop up roof, an English speaking driver guide, and a radio to help locate wildlife.	["Four nights in the Masai Mara timed for the Great Migration", "Three full days of game drives from sunrise to sunset", "Mara River crossing point visited during migration season", "Rhinos and flamingos at Lake Nakuru National Park", "Boat ride among hippos on Lake Naivasha", "Exclusive use of a 4x4 Land Cruiser with a pop up roof"]	["All park entrance fees", "Accommodation as per the itinerary on full board", "Bottled drinking water during the safari", "Services of an English speaking experienced driver guide", "Transport in a 4x4 safari Land Cruiser with pop up roof for game viewing and photography", "Exclusive use of the safari vehicle throughout the trip", "Meals as in the itinerary", "All government taxes and levies", "Safari accessories including a first aid kit, cooler box and fire extinguisher with a 24 hour emergency number", "All safari vehicles carry radio to help the driver locate wildlife"]	["Expenses of a personal nature such as visas and driver tips", "Personal insurance cover", "Alcoholic and non alcoholic drinks", "Domestic and international flights and respective taxes", "Soft drinks and local beers", "Optional hot air balloon ride in Masai Mara at 450 USD per person", "Optional Masai village visit at 25 USD per person", "Optional guided nature walk at 25 USD per person"]	[{"day": 1, "title": "Nairobi to Masai Mara National Reserve", "description": "Set off from your hotel or residence in Nairobi at 8 am, heading down into the Great Rift Valley with a quick stop to admire the view of the escarpment. Another stop in Narok town allows you to pick up any personal valuables you might need, as the driver also refuels the vehicle in this last town. Arrive at the Masai Mara in good time for lunch at the camp, giving you a chance to relax after the lengthy drive. Following lunch, you can choose from the various activities available at the camp, including a guided nature walk, a Masai village visit, or an afternoon game drive in the park to see the Big Five, all of which live in this wonderful game reserve. Dinner and overnight at Zebra Plains Mara Camp or similar."}, {"day": 2, "title": "Full Day Game Drive in Masai Mara", "description": "Have breakfast at 6 am and leave the camp with a packed picnic lunch at 6:30 am for a full day of game drives from 6:30 am to 6:30 pm. Spend the entire day exploring the reserve in search of the Big Five. With more than 450 bird species recorded here, there is much to see, including rhinos, leopards, elephants, buffalo, wildebeest, zebras, warthogs, jackals, lions, many types of antelopes, crocodiles and giraffes, whether you are a game lover or a birding enthusiast. Picnic lunch is served in the reserve along the banks of the Mara River, the wildebeest migration crossing point. Return to the camp in the evening for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 3, "title": "Full Day Game Drive in Masai Mara", "description": "After breakfast, leave for an early game drive from 6:30 am to 6:30 pm in search of wildlife you never got a chance to view the previous day, and gain more experiences, because you cannot predict nature and you will be covering different parts of the reserve. The Masai Mara is Kenya's most famous reserve due to its large population of wildlife, and it is one of the few places where all of the Big Five are found. The park also boasts 470 species of birds and rare animals like roan antelopes and nocturnal bat eared foxes, and you will also see the beautiful lilac breasted roller, which is Kenya's national bird. Back to the camp in the evening for dinner and overnight."}, {"day": 4, "title": "Full Day Game Drive in Masai Mara", "description": "Another full day in the reserve from 6:30 am to 6:30 pm, exploring fresh corners of the Mara that you have not yet visited. Each area of the reserve offers something different, from open plains where big cats roam to the riverine forest along the Mara River where hippos and crocodiles gather. Your driver guide uses the vehicle's radio to follow sightings across the park, giving you the best possible chance of witnessing a migration crossing when the herds are in season. Dinner and overnight at Zebra Plains Mara Camp or similar."}, {"day": 5, "title": "Masai Mara to Lake Nakuru National Park", "description": "After breakfast, leave the camp and depart for Lake Nakuru National Park, arriving in the mid morning with a lunch break at your lodge, followed by a safari game drive. Lake Nakuru gives you a chance of viewing hundreds of species of birds, including the lesser and greater flamingos and the pelicans. It is also a rhino sanctuary, and waterbucks, impala, buffalo and gazelle are found in the surrounding gardens. Dinner and overnight at Lake Nakuru Sopa Lodge or similar."}, {"day": 6, "title": "Lake Nakuru to Lake Naivasha and Nairobi", "description": "After breakfast, leave your lodge for a drive to Lake Naivasha, located in Kenya's Rift Valley and renowned for its dramatic landscapes. You will arrive in good time to explore Lake Naivasha on a boat ride tour, watching hippos in the water and birds along the shore through the entire afternoon. Leave for the drive back to Nairobi with sweet memories as your safari ends."}]	4.9	73	Daily	Easy	2-7 persons	private	midrange	f	f	29	2026-09-21 08:43:58.336549	aha	\N	\N
\.
